# nr-office-pdf-render-core: the page rasteriser of mixdog-pdf (src/render/)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave), and `render` is not a module of mixdog-pdf until the line below is applied.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod image;` (the last `pub mod` line of the module list) add:

    pub mod render;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], after `mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }` (mixdog-raster does not depend on mixdog-pdf: no cycle):

    mixdog-raster = { workspace = true }

The integration test tests/twin_render_core.rs uses mixdog-raster (Image::decode, Image::from_raw), mixdog-office-base (twin),
mixdog-testkit and serde_json, all already dependencies or dev-dependencies of the crate. No new external crate:
`cargo update --workspace --offline` and `cargo hakari generate` only add the edge mixdog-pdf -> mixdog-raster to the lock and to
mixdog-workspace-hack's feature unification if hakari wants it.

