## What the rasteriser needs from other tasks

- Fonts: `render::FontDrawing` is the seam of the font object that draws (`font(loaded_name)` and `glyph(loaded_name, glyph)` returning the
  outline path words of crate::glyph). Nothing in the tree implements `crate::oplist::FontProvider` or turns a font program into the
  outline of a glyph by its `fontChar` (pdf.js's repaired program and its cmap); until a task supplies both, `RenderOptions { fonts: None,
  drawing: None }` renders pages without text (and says so once).
- nr-office-pdf-render-paint (Type3, shadings, patterns, soft masks, groups, blend modes) extends `render::painter::Painter`
  (`pending_clip`, the `Extra` state, `Op::ShadingFill`, `Op::SetFillPattern`, `Op::BeginGroup`, the `type3` branch of `show_text`):
  it adds `mod shading; mod pattern; mod transparency;` to render/mod.rs.
- nr-office-pdf-render-pages calls `render::render_page` once per page on a `mixdog-rt` lane job, each job opening its own `Document`
  from the shared bytes, and passes the cancel check through `OpenOptions::cancel`.

No service, protocol method or SERVICE_PENDING name comes from this task.
